#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:3
msgid "AMDGPU Execution Synchronization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:8
msgid ""
"This document covers different ways of synchronizing execution of threads on "
"AMD GPUs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:11
msgid ""
"This document is not exhaustive. There may be more ways of synchronizing "
"execution that are not covered by this document."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:15
msgid "Barriers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:17
msgid ""
"This section covers execution synchronization using barrier-style primitives."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:21
msgid "Execution Model"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:23
msgid ""
"This section contains a formal execution model that can be used to model the "
"behavior of barriers on AMDGPU targets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:26
msgid ""
"Barriers only synchronize execution and do not affect the visibility of "
"memory operations between threads. Refer to the {ref}`execution barriers "
"memory model<amdgpu-amdhsa-execution-barriers-memory-model>` to determine "
"how to synchronize memory operations through *barrier-executes-before*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:31
msgid "The barrier execution model is experimental and subject to change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:34
#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:311
msgid "Barrier *Objects*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:37
msgid ""
"Threads can synchronize execution by performing barrier operations on "
"barrier *objects* as described below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:39
msgid "Each barrier *object* has the following state:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:41
msgid ""
"An unsigned positive integer *expected count*: counts the number of *arrive* "
"operations expected for this barrier *object*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:44
msgid ""
"An unsigned non-negative integer *arrive count*: counts the number of "
"*arrive* operations already performed on this barrier *object*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:47
msgid "The initial value of *arrive count* is zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:48
msgid ""
"When an operation causes *arrive count* to be equal to *expected count*, the "
"barrier is completed, and the *arrive count* is reset to zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:51
msgid ""
"Barrier *objects* exist within a *scope* instance (see {ref}`amdgpu-amdhsa-"
"llvm-sync-scopes-table`), and thus can only be accessed by threads in the "
"same *scope* instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:56
#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:320
msgid "Barrier Operations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:59
msgid ""
"Barrier operations are performed on barrier *objects*. A barrier operation "
"is a dynamic instance of one of the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:62
msgid "Barrier *init*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:64
msgid ""
"Barrier *init* takes an additional unsigned positive integer argument *k*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:65
msgid "Sets the *expected count* of the *barrier object* to *k*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:66
msgid "Resets the *arrive count* of the *barrier object* to zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:68
#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:90
msgid "Barrier *drop*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:70
msgid "Decrements *expected count* of the barrier *object* by one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:71
msgid ""
"A barrier *drop* cannot cause the *expected count* of the barrier *object* "
"to become negative; otherwise, the behavior is undefined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:74
#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:91
msgid "Barrier *arrive*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:76
msgid "Increments the *arrive count* of the barrier *object* by one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:77
msgid ""
"If supported, an additional argument to *arrive* can also update the "
"*expected count* of the barrier *object* before the *arrive count* is "
"incremented; the new *expected count* cannot be less than or equal to the "
"*arrive count*, otherwise the behavior is undefined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:82
msgid "Barrier *wait*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:84
msgid ""
"Introduces execution dependencies between threads; this operation depends on "
"other barrier operations to complete."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:87
msgid ""
"Barrier modification operations are barrier operations that modify the "
"barrier *object* state:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:89
msgid "Barrier *init*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:93
msgid "`Thread-barrier-order<BO>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:96
msgid ""
"`Thread-barrier-order<BO>` is the subset of *program-order* that only "
"relates barrier operations performed on a barrier *object* `BO`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:99
msgid "`Barrier-modification-order<BO>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:102
msgid ""
"All barrier modification operations on a barrier *object* `BO` occur in a "
"strict total order called `barrier-modification-order<BO>`; it is the order "
"in which `BO` observes barrier operations that change its state. For any "
"valid `barrier-modification-order<BO>`, the following must be true:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:107
msgid ""
"Let `A` and `B` be two barrier modification operations where `A -> B` in "
"`thread-barrier-order<BO>`, then `A -> B` is also in `barrier-modification-"
"order<BO>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:109
msgid ""
"The first element in `barrier-modification-order<BO>` is always a barrier "
"*init*, otherwise the behavior is undefined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:112
msgid "*Barrier-participates-in*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:115
msgid ""
"*Barrier-participates-in* relates barrier operations to the barrier *waits* "
"that depend on them to complete. A barrier operation `X` *barrier-"
"participates-in* a barrier *wait* `W` if and only if all of the following is "
"true:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:119
msgid "`X` and `W` are both performed on the same barrier *object* `BO`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:120
msgid "`X` is a barrier *arrive* or *drop* operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:121
msgid ""
"`X` does not *barrier-participate-in* another distinct barrier *wait* `W'` "
"in the same thread as `W`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:122
msgid "`W -> X` not in `thread-barrier-order<BO>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:123
msgid "All dependent constraint and relations are satisfied as well. [^0]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:125
msgid ""
"For the set `S` consisting of all barrier operations that *barrier-"
"participate-in* a barrier *wait* `W` for some barrier *object* `BO`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:128
msgid ""
"The elements of `S` all exist in a continuous, uninterrupted interval of "
"`barrier-modification-order<BO>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:129
msgid ""
"The *arrive count* of `BO` is zero before the first operation of `S` in "
"`barrier-modification-order<BO>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:130
msgid ""
"The *arrive count* and *expected count* of `BO` are equal after the last "
"operation of `S` in `barrier-modification-order<BO>`. The *arrive count* and "
"*expected count* of `BO` cannot equal at any other point in `S`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:139
msgid "*Barrier-executes-before*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:142
msgid ""
"A barrier operation `A` *barrier-executes-before* another barrier operation "
"`B` if any of the following is true:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:145
msgid "`A -> B` in *program-order*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:146
msgid "`A -> B` in *barrier-participates-in*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:147
msgid ""
"`A` *barrier-executes-before* some barrier operation `X`, and `X` *barrier-"
"executes-before* `B`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:150
msgid ""
"*Barrier-executes-before* is consistent with `barrier-modification-"
"order<BO>` for every barrier object `BO`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:152
msgid "Barrier *drop* races"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:155
msgid ""
"For every pair of barrier *arrive* `A` and barrier *drop* `D` performed on a "
"barrier *object* `BO`, such that `A -> D` in `thread-barrier-order<BO>`, one "
"of the following must be true:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:158
msgid "`A` does not *barrier-participates-in* any barrier *wait*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:159
msgid ""
"`A` *barrier-participates-in* at least one barrier *wait* `W` such that `W -"
"> D` in *barrier-executes-before*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:162
msgid "*barrier-phase-with*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:165
msgid ""
"*barrier-phase-with* is a symmetric relation over barrier operations defined "
"as the transitive closure of: *barrier-participates-in* and its inverse "
"relation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:168
msgid "Barrier phase separation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:171
msgid ""
"For every barrier operation `A` that *barrier-participates-in* a barrier "
"*wait* `W` on a barrier *object* `BO`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:173
msgid ""
"There is no barrier operation `X` on `BO` such that `A -> X -> W` in "
"*barrier-executes-before*, and `X` *barrier-phase-with* a non-empty set of "
"operations that does not include `W`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:177
msgid "Informational Notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:179
msgid ""
"Informally, we can deduce from the above formal model that execution "
"barriers behave as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:181
msgid ""
"*Barrier-executes-before* relates the dynamic instances of operations from "
"different threads together. For example, if `A -> B` in *barrier-executes-"
"before*, then the execution of `A` must complete before the execution of `B` "
"can complete."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:185
msgid ""
"This property can also be combined with *program-order*. For example, let "
"two (non-barrier) operations `X` and `Y` where `X -> A` and `B -> Y` in "
"*program-order*, then we know that the execution of `X` completes before the "
"execution of `Y` does."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:189
msgid ""
"Barriers do not complete \"out-of-thin-air\"; a barrier *wait* `W` cannot "
"depend on a barrier operation `X` to complete if `W -> X` in *barrier-"
"executes-before*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:192
msgid "It is undefined behavior to operate on an uninitialized barrier object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:194
msgid "It is undefined behavior for a barrier *wait* to never complete."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:196
msgid "It is not mandatory to *drop* a barrier after *joining* it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:198
msgid ""
"A thread may not *arrive* and then *drop* a barrier *object* unless the "
"barrier completes before the barrier *drop*. Incrementing the *arrive count* "
"and decrementing the *expected count* directly after may cause undefined "
"behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:202
msgid ""
"*Joining* a barrier is only useful if the thread will *wait* on that same "
"barrier *object* later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:204
msgid "Barrier Implementations on AMDGPU Targets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:206
#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:258
#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:266
msgid "`s_barrier`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:208
msgid "`s_barrier` are the primary barrier implementation of AMD GPUs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:210
msgid ""
"`s_barrier` instructions can only be used to synchronize threads at a "
"wavefront granularity. `s_barrier` instructions are convergent within a "
"wave, and thus can only be performed in wave-uniform control flow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:214
msgid ""
"The `s_barrier` family of instructions is available in some form on all GFX "
"targets, and has evolved over time. The sub-sections below cover the "
"capabilities offered by every major iteration of this feature separately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:218
msgid "GFX6-11"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:220
msgid ""
"Targets from GFX6 through GFX11 included do not have the \"split barrier\" "
"feature. The barrier *arrive* and barrier *wait* operations **cannot** be "
"performed independently using `s_barrier`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:224
msgid ""
"There is only one *workgroup barrier* object of `workgroup` scope that is "
"implicitly used by all `s_barrier` instructions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:227
msgid ""
"The following code sequences can be used to implement the barrier operations "
"defined by the {ref}`execution synchronization model<amdgpu-execution-"
"synchronization-barriers-execution-model>` using `s_barrier` on GFX6 through "
"GFX11:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:231
msgid "s_barrier GFX6-11"
msgstr ""

