msgid "AMDGPU Machine Code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:239
msgid "**Init and Drop**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:242
#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:378
#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:383
#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:388
#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:393
msgid "*init*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:243
#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:248
#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:255
#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:277
#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:280
msgid "*Workgroup barrier*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:244
#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:380
msgid ""
"Automatically initialized by the hardware when a workgroup is launched. The "
"*expected count* of this barrier is set to the number of waves in the "
"workgroup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:247
#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:412
#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:424
msgid "*drop*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:249
#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:428
msgid ""
"When a thread ends, it automatically *drops* this barrier *object* if it had "
"previously *joined* it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:251
#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:430
msgid "**Arrive and Wait**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:254
msgid "*arrive* then *wait*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:256
msgid "**BackOffBarrier**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:260
msgid "**No BackOffBarrier**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:262
msgid "`s_waitcnt vmcnt(0) expcnt(0) lgkmcnt(0)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:264
msgid "`s_waitcnt_vscnt null, 0x0`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:268
msgid ""
"If the target does not have the BackOffBarrier feature, then there cannot be "
"any outstanding memory operations before issuing the `s_barrier` instruction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:271
msgid ""
"The waitcnts can independently be moved earlier, or removed entirely as long "
"as the associated counter remains at zero before issuing the `s_barrier` "
"instruction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:274
msgid ""
"The `s_barrier` instruction cannot complete before all waves of the "
"workgroup have launched."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:276
#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:433
msgid "*arrive*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:278
#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:281
msgid "Not available separately, see *arrive* then *wait*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:279
#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:461
msgid "*wait*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:284
msgid "GFX12"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:286
msgid ""
"GFX12 targets have the split-barrier feature, and also allow `s_barrier` "
"instructions to use one of multiple barrier *objects* available per "
"workgroup. `s_barrier` instruction use the barrier ID operand to determine "
"the barrier *object* they operate on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:290
msgid ""
"GFX12.5 additionally introduces new barrier *objects* that offer more "
"flexibility for synchronizing the execution of a subset of waves of a "
"workgroup, or synchronizing execution across workgroups within a workgroup "
"cluster, via `s_barrier`. These are called \"named barriers\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:295
msgid ""
"Check the {ref}`the table below<amdgpu-execution-synchronization-barriers-"
"sbarrier-ids-gfx12>` to determine which barrier IDs are available to "
"`s_barrier` instructions on a given target."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:301
msgid "\"Named Barriers\" Model Extensions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:303
msgid ""
"In order to reason about the execution of `s_barrier` \"named barriers\" on "
"GFX12.5 and up, we define the following extensions to the {ref}`barrier "
"execution model<amdgpu-execution-synchronization-barriers-execution-model>`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:308
msgid ""
"The aforementioned execution model always applies unless stated otherwise by "
"one of the extensions below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:314
msgid ""
"There is a sub-type of barrier *objects* called *named barrier objects*. "
"*Named barrier objects* inherit all the properties of barrier *objects* as "
"defined by the barrier execution model. They are also subject to additional "
"constraints."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:318
msgid ""
"Not all barrier *objects* are *named barrier objects*, and both types can "
"coexist in an implementation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:323
msgid ""
"The entirety of the {ref}`barrier operations section<amdgpu-execution-"
"synchronization-barriers-execution-model-barrier-operations>` applies, with "
"the following barrier operation being added:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:327
msgid "Barrier *join*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:329
msgid ""
"Allow the thread that executes the operation to *wait* on a barrier *object*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:330
msgid "Can only be used on *named barrier objects*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:332
msgid "*Barrier-joined-before*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:335
msgid ""
"A barrier *join* `J` is *barrier-joined-before* a barrier operation `X` if "
"and only if all of the following is true:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:338
msgid "`J -> X` in `thread-barrier-order<BO>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:339
msgid "`X` is not a barrier *join*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:340
msgid ""
"There is no barrier *join* or *drop* `JD` where `J -> JD -> X` in `thread-"
"barrier-order<BO>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:341
msgid ""
"There is no barrier *join* `J'` on a distinct barrier *object* `BO'` such "
"that `J -> J' -> X` in *program-order*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:344
msgid "Join and Drop Ordering"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:347
msgid ""
"For every barrier *drop* `D` performed on a *named barrier object* `BO`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:349
msgid ""
"There is a barrier *join* `J` such that `J -> D` in *barrier-joined-before*; "
"otherwise, the behavior is undefined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:352
msgid "Join and Wait Ordering"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:355
msgid ""
"For every barrier *wait* `W` performed on a *named barrier object* `BO`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:357
msgid ""
"There is a barrier *join* `J` such that `J -> W` in *barrier-joined-before*, "
"and `J` must *barrier-executes-before* at least one operation `X` that "
"*barrier-participates-in* `W`; otherwise, the behavior is undefined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:361
msgid "Code Sequences"
msgstr ""

