"The value to set as the *expected count* of the barrier is stored in the "
"upper half of `m0`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:400
#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:405
msgid "*join*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:404
msgid "N/A"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:409
msgid "`s_barrier_join <N>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:416
msgid "`s_barrier_leave`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:418
msgid ""
"`s_barrier_leave` takes no operand. It can only be used to *drop* a *named* "
"barrier *object* `BO` if `BO` was previously *joined* using `s_barrier_join`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:421
msgid ""
"*Drops* the *named* barrier *object* `BO` if and only if there is a barrier "
"*join* `J` such that `J` is *barrier-joined-before* this barrier *drop* "
"operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:441
msgid "`s_barrier_signal <N>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:443
msgid "Or"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:445
msgid "`s_barrier_signal_isfirst <N>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:447
msgid "`<N>` is an immediate constant, or stored in bits `[4:0]` of `m0`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:448
msgid ""
"The `_isfirst` variant sets `SCC=1` if this wave is the first to signal the "
"barrier, otherwise `SCC=0`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:450
msgid ""
"For barrier *objects* `[1, 16]`: When using `m0` as an operand, if there is "
"a non-zero value contained in the bits `[22:16]` of `m0`, the *expected "
"count* of the barrier *object* is set to that value before the *arrive "
"count* of the barrier *object* is incremented. The new *expected count* "
"value must be greater than or equal to the *arrive count*, otherwise the "
"behavior is undefined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:456
msgid ""
"For barrier *objects* `-4` and `-3` (`cluster` barriers): only one wave per "
"workgroup may arrive at the barrier on behalf of its entire workgroup. "
"However, any wave within the workgroup cluster can then *wait* on this "
"barrier *object*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:460
#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:477
msgid "This is a no-op on the *NULL barrier* (barrier *object* `0`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:469
msgid "`s_barrier_wait <N>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:471
msgid "`<N>` is an immediate constant."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:472
msgid ""
"For barrier *objects* `-2` and `-1`: This instruction cannot complete before "
"all waves of the workgroup have launched."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:474
msgid ""
"For barrier *objects* `-4` and `-3` (`cluster` barriers): This instruction "
"cannot complete before all waves of the workgroup cluster have launched."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:478
msgid ""
"For *named barrier objects*, this instruction always waits on the last "
"*named barrier object* that the thread has *joined*, even if it is different "
"from the *barrier object* passed to the instruction."
msgstr ""

