msgid ""
"All operations on the *NULL named barrier object* other than *join* are no-"
"ops."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:536
msgid ""
"As the *NULL barrier* (barrier ID `0`) is also a *named* barrier *object*, a "
"thread can use a *join* on the *NULL* barrier as a way to \"unjoin\" a "
"*named barrier* (break *barrier-joined-before*) without having to use a "
"*drop* operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:540
msgid ""
"When a thread ends, it does **not** implicitly *drop* any *named barrier "
"objects* (barrier IDs `[0, 16]`) it has *joined*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.md:134
msgid ""
"The definition of *barrier-participates-in* (in its current state) is non-"
"deterministic and will be improved in the future: Within a valid execution, "
"there may be multiple ways to build *barrier-participates-in*, however there "
"is only one way to build it that also satisfies all other relations and "
"constraints that depend on *barrier-participates-in* and relations derived "
"from it."
msgstr ""
